<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.DocumentFormat
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:diag="org.blockml.bml.diagnostic"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>DocumentFormat</name>
  <type>doc:DocumentFormat</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to the BML document root format</is>

  <summary>A .bml document root is the Block type tag. Legacy &lt;block&gt; plus &lt;type&gt;
    remains valid during a long transition. xmlns:xsi and xsi:schemaLocation are omitted by
    default — validation is the validator and LSP, not XSD.</summary>

  <documentation><![CDATA[
    A `.bml` file is one XML document. The root element identifies the Block being defined.
    Two authoring formats are valid during a long transition. The type-as-root-tag form is the
    intended long-term format; the legacy `<block>` form remains valid until it is withdrawn.

    Existing sources in this library stay in the legacy form until they are migrated.

    ## Qualified root (recommended)

    Legacy:

        <block>
          <name>MyBlock</name>  <!-- optional -->
          <type>acme:MyBlock</type>
          …
        </block>

    Preferred:

        <acme:MyBlock>
          <name>MyBlock</name>  <!-- optional -->
          …
        </acme:MyBlock>

    The root QName is the type. Prefixes resolve via xmlns Package bindings
    (doc:BmlNamespace). Child `<type>` is omitted when the root tag already supplies the type.
    Optional `<name>` must still equal `lastSegment(resolve(type))` when present
    (BML_BLOCK_NAME_TYPE_MISMATCH).

    ## Unqualified root

    Legacy:

        <block>
          <name>MyBlock</name>
          …
        </block>

    Preferred:

        <MyBlock>
          <name>MyBlock</name>  <!-- optional, not recommended -->
          …
        </MyBlock>

    The local name of the root tag is the type (and the effective name). A redundant `<name>`
    is allowed but not recommended. Unqualified roots follow the same identity rules as
    unqualified type references (doc:TypeIdentityDerivation / doc:ImplicitNamespaceResolution).

    ## Dual format

    Parser, validator, and LSP accept both forms. New documents should use the type-as-root-tag
    form. Both remain valid until the legacy form is withdrawn.

    Identity rules (doc:TypeIdentityDerivation) are unchanged:

    • type is required as canonical identity — supplied by the root tag and/or child `<type>`
    • name remains optional and must match `lastSegment(resolve(type))` when present
    • BML_MISSING_BLOCK_TYPE when neither the root tag nor `<type>` supplies a type
      (legacy `<block>` without `<type>`)
    • when both the root tag and `<type>` supply a type, they must resolve to the same FQN

    A generic `<block>` root is not itself a type. In the legacy form, identity comes from
    `<type>` (and optional `<name>`). In the preferred form the root tag *is* the type, so
    `<type>` is omitted.

    Inner members, Sub-Blocks, and instance children are unchanged. Instance serialization
    already uses the declared type tag (`<core:Block>`, `<myns:Wall>`).

    ## XSD is not a standard feature

    `xmlns:xsi` and `xsi:schemaLocation` are omitted by default. XML Schema is not an officially
    supported standard feature. The XSD compiler remains available; it is not used by default.
    Semantic validation is the validator and the LSP.

    Default `xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"` and BML-semantic prefixes stay. Other URI bindings
    (schemaLocation keys) are not BML-semantic type namespaces (doc:BmlNamespace).
    `Library.schemas` remains an optional legacy catalog of XSD paths during migration
    (doc:LibrarySystem).
  ]]></documentation>

